sentences.text:
In this writ petition, the petitioners have sought for the following reliefs:-
(i) Issue writ of certiorari to quash the award passed by the 1st respondent for Tenkayedapadavu village of Gurupura Hobli, Mangalore Taluk, D.K. District dated 30.01.2021 produced as Annexure-E;
(ii) Writ of Mandamus directing the 1st respondent strictly in accordance with Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013;
(iii) Under the facts and circumstances of the present case, to grant such other relief/s as this Hon'ble Court would deem fit to be granted in the interest of justice and equity.

7. In the result, I pass the following order:-
ORDER i) Writ petition is disposed off;
ii) The dispute involved in the present petition with regard to quantum of compensation payable to the petitioners as well as the legality, validity and correctness of the impugned awards are hereby referred to the Deputy Sri Madhava S/O Nagappa Devadiga vs Special Land Acquisition Officer

6 Commissioner/ Statutory Arbitrator before whom, the petitions filed by the respondents challenging the first / original awards passed by the respondents which were subject matter of Valerial Sequeria's case (supra) are pending adjudication for disposal in accordance with law iii) The Deputy Commissioner/ Statutory Arbitrator before whom the aforesaid petitions filed by the respondents are pending, is hereby directed to club / tag the dispute involved in the present writ petition also along with pending petitions and dispose of the same together in accordance with law;
iv) Liberty is reserved in favour of the petitioners herein to file pleadings, documents,
etc. in the matters referred to the Deputy Commissioner/ Statutory Arbitrator pursuant to this order;
- 10 - v) All rival contentions are kept open and no opinion is expressed on the same;
vi) The Deputy Commissioner/ Statutory Arbitrator is directed to dispose of all the proceedings including the proceedings referred to under this order, within a period of six months from the date of receipt of a copy of this order;
vii) It is made clear that this order is restricted to the petitioners only and is made in the peculiar/
special facts and circumstances of the instant case and shall not be treated as a precedent nor having any precedential value for any purpose whatsoever.
Sd/-
